    "context.logSources.4.description": "Name of the exercise terminal or log collector. It may differ from the server names that produced individual logs.",
    "context.logSources.5.description": "Exercise overview and operating instructions. Supporting material, not an audit event.",
    "context.assumptions.0": "All data is synthetic and imitates records from Linux services. No real OS or Web, SSH, DNS, or mail servers are running. The terminal operates on virtual files in the browser and supports only the implemented commands.",
    "context.assumptions.1": "The Normal and Reproduce attack logs actions switch between prepared static logs. They cause no external communication, real attacks, or execution of commands found in logs. IP addresses, domains, and accounts are also training data.",
    "context.assumptions.2": "Check the time format for each log. Z and +0000 mean UTC; +0900 means Japan time. If syslog omits the year or zone, use the README collection notes and normalize to UTC before correlating.",
